<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila call rate up as special bills sap liquidity.</title>
<headline>Manila call rate up as special bills sap liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>----------------------- Sept 16 -------------------------</p>
<p>* Interbank call average inches up to 11.125 pct</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Philippine overnight money inched up on Monday to 11.125 percent from Friday's 11.03125 percent as the peso supply dwindled slightly after banks parked their funds in special series Treasury bills, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Many banks went into the special series bills on fear that the Central Bank might lower its rates when the auction rates come out this afternoon,&quot; one trader said.</p>
</text>
